{"slug":"decisions-0002-npm-dist-tag","title":"ADR 0002 — npm dist-tag publish wiring","blocks":[
{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"On 2026-04-19, a release run published two pre-release artifacts to the wrong npm dist-tag, landing a pre-release version on the default-resolved "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" channel."}]},
{"id":"b2","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Status:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Accepted"}]},
{"id":"b3","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Date:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" 2026-04-19"}]},
{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Deciders:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Barkpark core team"}]},
{"id":"b5","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Related:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" P0 incident — release.yml run 24627335562; defects #16, #18; ADR 0001"}]},
{"id":"b6","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Context"},
{"id":"b7","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"On 2026-04-19, release.yml run "},{"type":"text","value":"24627335562","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" published two pre-release artifacts to the wrong npm dist-tag:"}]},
{"id":"b8","type":"table","head":[
[{"type":"text","value":"Package"}],
[{"type":"text","value":"preview"}],
[{"type":"text","value":"latest"}]
],"rows":[
[[{"type":"text","value":"@barkpark/core","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0-preview.0"}],[{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0-preview.1","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"  (should be preview)"}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"@barkpark/nextjs","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0-preview.0"}],[{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0-preview.1","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"  (should be preview)"}]]
]},
{"id":"b9","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"A pre-release version landed on "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", the channel that "},{"type":"text","value":"npm install","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" resolves by default. Local "},{"type":"text","value":"npm dist-tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" retag attempts return HTTP 403 — only the CI NPM_TOKEN holds publish/dist-tag scope on "},{"type":"text","value":"@barkpark/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Any fix must therefore run inside a GitHub Actions workflow."}]},
{"id":"b10","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What the wiring actually does"},
{"id":"b11","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/release.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" exposes a "},{"type":"text","value":"dist_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"workflow_dispatch","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" input (values: "},{"type":"text","value":"preview | next | latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", default "},{"type":"text","value":"preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") and computes "},{"type":"text","value":"steps.mode.outputs.dist_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" from it. That value is then used "},{"type":"text","value":"only","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" for log lines ("},{"type":"text","value":"::warning::","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" notice and "},{"type":"text","value":"$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). It is "},{"type":"text","value":"not","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" passed to the publish CLI."}]},
{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The \"Publish (REAL — emits to npm)\" step runs:"}]},
{"id":"b13","type":"code","value":"pnpm changeset publish"},
{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"with no "},{"type":"text","value":"--tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" flag. The inline comment is explicit about why:"}]},
{"id":"b15","type":"callout","tone":"info","content":[{"type":"text","value":"NOTE: no --tag here. Pre-mode ("},{"type":"text","value":".changeset/pre.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"tag=\"preview\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") auto-applies the dist-tag; passing --tag explicitly fails with \"Releasing under custom tag is not allowed in pre mode\"."}]},
{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"So the published dist-tag is governed entirely by "},{"type":"text","value":"js/.changeset/pre.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — specifically its "},{"type":"text","value":"\"tag\": \"preview\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" field — "},{"type":"text","value":"whenever pre-mode is active on the publishing commit","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". If pre-mode is "},{"type":"text","value":"not","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" active at publish time ("},{"type":"text","value":"pre.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" absent, or "},{"type":"text","value":"changeset pre exit","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" already run, or the package not covered by the active pre-mode set), "},{"type":"text","value":"changeset publish","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" falls back to its default behavior, which is to publish under "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"text","value":"dist_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" workflow input has no path to override that fallback; it is purely informational."}]},
{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"This is the wiring gap that produced the incident: the operator selected "},{"type":"text","value":"dist_tag=preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on the dispatch form and reasonably assumed that selection governed the publish. It did not. The publish landed on whatever pre-mode (or its absence) implied — "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" in this case."}]},
{"id":"b18","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Decision"},
{"id":"b19","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"Immediate fix (this PR):","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" ship "},{"type":"text","value":".github/workflows/retag.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — a "},{"type":"text","value":"workflow_dispatch","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"-only workflow that performs "},{"type":"text","value":"npm dist-tag add","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and a guarded "},{"type":"text","value":"npm dist-tag rm","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" from CI, where NPM_TOKEN has the required scope rights. The remove step is hard-guarded against the protected channels "},{"type":"text","value":"preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"next","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":": if either is supplied, the step is "},{"type":"text","value":"skipped with a warning, not failed","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — protected channels are how downstream installs subscribe to the pre-release stream, and silently yanking them would break every consumer tracking them."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"Do not modify ","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"release.yml","marks":["code","strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" in this PR.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" The retag workflow is the surgical remediation; the release-wiring fix belongs in a separately reviewed change so the rollback story for this incident stays narrow."}]
]},
{"id":"b20","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Consequences"},
{"id":"b21","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"The inverted dist-tag state can be corrected by a single operator running "},{"type":"text","value":"retag.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" once per affected package: "},{"type":"text","value":"add_tag=preview","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"version=1.0.0-preview.1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"remove_tag=","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (empty — "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" will be moved by the "},{"type":"text","value":"add","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" of the correct version when the next real release lands; we do not strip "},{"type":"text","value":"latest","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" mid-incident because that would break "},{"type":"text","value":"npm install","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" resolution for users who already pinned to it)."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"text","value":"dist_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" input on "},{"type":"text","value":"release.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" continues to be a footgun until follow-up work lands. Until then, operators must understand that the effective publish tag is determined by "},{"type":"text","value":"js/.changeset/pre.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", not the workflow input."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"retag.yml","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is a general-purpose remediation tool and will outlive this incident — it is the right escape hatch any time npm dist-tag state and intent diverge."}]
]},
{"id":"b22","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Recommended follow-up (separate PR — NOT in scope here)"},
{"id":"b23","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire the "},{"type":"text","value":"dist_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" input through to the publish CLI so the dispatch form selection actually matters:"}]},
{"id":"b24","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"When pre-mode is active","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"text","value":"js/.changeset/pre.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" exists): keep the current behavior — pre.json's "},{"type":"text","value":"tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is canonical, refuse to override, and fail loudly if "},{"type":"text","value":"dist_tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" disagrees with "},{"type":"text","value":"pre.json.tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" so the mismatch is caught at dispatch time rather than after publish."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"When pre-mode is not active","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":": pass "},{"type":"text","value":"--tag \"${dist_tag}\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"text","value":"pnpm changeset publish","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (or, equivalently, "},{"type":"text","value":"pnpm publish -r --tag ...","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" for the workspace), and validate the input is one of the documented channels."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"Add an explicit assertion step that reads "},{"type":"text","value":"pre.json","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and reconciles it against the input "},{"type":"text","value":"before","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" the publish step runs — so the operator gets a clear error in the workflow log, not a wrong-channel publish in npm."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"Consider exiting pre-mode ("},{"type":"text","value":"changeset pre exit","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") before publishing the GA "},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" so the post-pre-exit publish path is exercised before it becomes load-bearing."}]
]}
],"related":["decisions-0001-sdk-envelope"]}
